    "name": "William & Mary Computer Science Student Advisory Council",
    "description": "From my role as ACM Chair at William & Mary, I have found that there is a lack of communication between these current undergraduate students within the computer science department and the faculty of this department. This is largely because there is currently no formalized avenue for the\ndepartment to gauge student response or for students to provide feedback. At the 2018 Richard Tapia Conference I was introduced to the idea of CS Student advisory committees, which would fit this need. Working with Robert Michael Lewis, the William & Mary Computer Science department's chair, I am seeking to found such a body. ",
